The {{nihongo|'''Imaichi Line'''|今市線|Imaichi-sen}} is a subway line in [[Okami|Okami (大紙)]], [[Okaiken]], operated by [[Okami Metro]]. It functions as a strategic connector line, linking the southern commercial hub of [[Ebisu-Miyoshi Station|Ebisu-Miyoshi]] with the northeastern residential districts of [[Itakano-Kita Station|Itakano-Kita]]. On system maps, the line is color-coded light brown ({{Okami Metro color|I}}), and its stations use the prefix "I".

Like the [[Nagata Line]], the Imaichi Line utilizes Linear Motor propulsion. This technology allows the line to utilize smaller tunnels and navigate the sharp turns required to thread through the already developed underground infrastructure of central and eastern Okami. It serves as a vital bypass, connecting multiple radial lines (Miyoshi, Chūō, Nagata, Kita) without requiring passengers to pass through the overcrowded [[Okami Central Station]].



==History==
The Imaichi Line is one of the newest additions to the Okami Metro network. Planned in the late 1990s as the "Eastern Corridor Rail Link," it was designed to address the "railway vacuum" in the eastern wards of [[Higashinari Ward, Okami|Higashinari]] and [[Asahi Ward, Okami|Asahi]].

Construction began in 2000, employing deep-bore tunneling techniques. The entire 11-station line opened simultaneously on December 24, 2006. Since its opening, it has spurred significant residential redevelopment in the [[Itakano]] area, transforming it from a quiet outskirt into a bustling commuter bed-town.

